{"id":"u-e54057dd-3b5c-455e-b115-2dd6818ed35f","src":"community","title":"DC Training 16 Week","author":"Andrew Girgis","url":"https://www.boostcamp.app/users/BLKsjx-dc-training-16-week","desc":"DC TRAINING – 16 WEEK IMPROVEMENT\n\nWHAT IS DC?\nDC (\"DoggCrapp\") Training was created by Dante Trudel, a bodybuilding coach and the founder of True Nutrition. It spread on bodybuilding forums in the early 2000s and built many competitive and pro bodybuilders. The core idea: strength gains drive size. Each muscle gets ONE all-out working set, trained more often, and you must beat your logbook every session. Fewer sets, more effort, more frequent growth signals.\n\nTHE 2-WAY SPLIT\nDay A: Chest, Shoulders, Triceps, Back Width, Back Thickness\nDay B: Biceps, Forearms, Calves, Hamstrings, Quads\n\nEach day has 3 exercise rotations (A1/A2/A3, B1/B2/B3), so you never repeat the same movement back to back and can keep adding load.\n\nA1: Incline Smith Press, Smith Military, Close-Grip Smith Bench, Chin-Ups, Deadlift\nA2: Machine Incline, DB Shoulder Press, Close-Grip Bench, Close-Grip Pulldown, T-Bar Row\nA3: Flat Bench, Plate-Loaded Shoulder Press, Skull Crusher, Lat Pulldown, BB Row\nB1: BB Curl, Hammer Curl, Standing Calf, Lying Leg Curl, Hack Squat\nB2: Alt DB Curl, Reverse EZ Curl, Leg Press Calf, RDL, Pendulum Squat\nB3: Cable Curl, Wrist Curl, Smith Calf, Seated Leg Curl, Leg Press\n\n16-WEEK LAYOUT\nWeeks 1–7, Blast 1 (3 days/week): Alternate A and B days. Each muscle is hit 3x every 2 weeks. Week 1 is for finding your weights. Go all-out from the second time you see each workout.\nWeeks 8–9, Cruise (3 days/week): A1 and B1 exercises, 2 sets of 8–10 at about 80% of blast weights, RPE 7. No failure. Drop one meal per day. This lets joints and recovery catch up so Blast 2 starts fresh.\nWeeks 10–16, Blast 2 (4 days/week): Each muscle is hit 2x per week. If your logbook stalls, drop back to 3 days.\n\nHOW EACH SET WORKS\nRest-pause (most lifts): Use a weight you can get 7–10 reps with. Go to failure, take 15 deep breaths, go to failure, take 15 breaths, then go to failure again. Aim for 11–15 total reps (15–25 for hamstrings). Hit the top of the range, then add weight.\nQuads: A heavy set of 4–8, rest 3–5 min, then a 20-rep widowmaker.\nBack thickness: A heavy set of 6–8, then a back-off set of 10–12. No rest-pause. Stop deadlifts 1 rep short of failure.\nCalves: 10–12 reps, with a 5-second negative and a 15-second stretch at the bottom of each rep.\nStraight sets: 1 set to failure in the listed range.\nControl every negative for 3–5 seconds.\n\nEXTREME STRETCH\nRight after each muscle's working set (except calves), hold a loaded stretch for 60–90 seconds. Examples: DB flye bottom for chest, dead hang for lats, deep sissy squat hold for quads. Don't skip it.\n\nLOGBOOK RULE\nLog every working set. Beat each exercise by 1 rep or 5 lb. If you miss twice in a row, swap the exercise.\n\nOFF DAYS\nFasted morning walk, 45–60 min. Eat 1.5–2 g protein per lb and drink plenty of water. Eat carbs earlier in the day and post-workout. No extra lifting, since recovery is what lets you beat the logbook.\n\nAFTER WEEK 16\nCruise for 10–14 days before the next blast.","level":["Intermediate"],"goals":["Muscle","Strength"],"equipment":["Full Gym"],"minutes":50,"joins":1,"rate":0,"rateCount":0,"updated":"2026-10-29T13:08:57.863Z","variations":[{"name":"default","days":["B2","B1","A2","B2"],"weeks":[[{"ex":[{"ss":[{"n":"Incline Bench Press (Smith Machine)","sets":[{"amrap":1,"x":3}]},{"n":"Seated Military Press (Smith Machine)","sets":[{"amrap":1,"x":3}]},{"n":"Close Grip Bench Press (Smith Machine)","sets":[{"amrap":1,"x":3}]},{"n":"Chin-Up (Bodyweight)","sets":[{"amrap":1,"x":3}]}]},{"n":"Deadlift (Barbell)","sets":[{"lo":6,"hi":8},{"lo":9,"hi":12}]}]},{"ex":[{"n":"Bicep Curl (Barbell)","sets":[{"amrap":1,"x":3}]},{"n":"Hammer Curl (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"lo":10,"hi":20}]},{"n":"Standing Calf Raise","sets":[{"lo":10,"hi":12}]},{"n":"Lying Leg Curl","se